mmand copied</string><string name="hc_graphics_api">Graphics API</string><string name="hc_graphics_api_about">What this does</string><string name="hc_graphics_api_about_summary">Forces Android’s UI renderer (HWUI / Skia) to Vulkan or OpenGL ES, the same debug.hwui.renderer switch used by GAMA. Vulkan often uses less power and runs cooler; OpenGL is the fallback if Vulkan glitches. Apps and games can still pick their own API. A reboot clears the property unless restore on boot is on and Shizuku or root is available. If the screen freezes, hold Volume down and Power.</string><string name="hc_graphics_applied">Renderer applied. Some screens may need a reboot.</string><string name="hc_graphics_copy_adb">Copy ADB command</string><string name="hc_graphics_current">Active renderer</string><string name="hc_graphics_default">System default</string><string name="hc_graphics_need_privilege">Could not apply. Grant Shizuku, use root, or run:\n%1$s</string><string name="hc_graphics_opengl">OpenGL</string><string name="hc_graphics_priv_missing">No Shizuku or root — use ADB</string><string name="hc_graphics_priv_ok">Shizuku or root ready</string><string name="hc_graphics_renderer">Renderer</string><string name="hc_graphics_renderer_summary">Needs Shizuku, root, or ADB (copy the command below)</string><string name="hc_graphics_restore_boot">Restore after reboot</string><string name="hc_graphics_restore_boot_summary">Re-applies Vulkan or OpenGL after boot when Shizuku or root is available. Android always clears the property on reboot.</string><string name="hc_graphics_unknown">Unknown</string><string name="hc_graphics_vulkan">Vulkan</string><string name="hc_graphics_widget_locked">Turn on “Switch from System widget” in Settings → Advanced → Graphics API first</string><string name="hc_graphics_widget_switch">Switch from System widget</string><string name="hc_graphics_widget_switch_summary">Lets the home-screen System widget change Vulkan or OpenGL. Off by default. Needs Shizuku, root,